We want to reduce the number of odd counts to $\le 1$.
Each removal of a character with an odd count reduces the number of odd counts by 1.
Each removal of a character with an even count increases the number of odd counts by 1.
We want to perform $k$ removals.
To minimize the final number of odd counts, we should prioritize removing characters that currently have odd counts.
Suppose we remove $x$ characters with odd counts. Then we must remove $k - x$ characters with even counts.
The final number of odd counts will be $odd\_count - x + (k - x) = odd\_count + k - 2x$.
